# Spec Workflow

This project uses a spec-driven development workflow (requirements → design → tasks → implementation).

## Locations

- Spec documents: `.cursor/specs/{feature_name}/` (kebab-case feature names, e.g. `user-authentication`)
  - `requirements.md` — EARS-format requirements
  - `design.md` — feature design document
  - `tasks.md` — implementation task checklist
- Workflow system prompt: `.cursor/system-prompts/spec-workflow-starter.md`
- Sub-agent definitions: `.cursor/agents/kfc/`
- Workflow settings: `.cursor/settings/kfc-settings.json`

## Conventions

- When starting a spec workflow, read `.cursor/system-prompts/spec-workflow-starter.md` first and follow it.
- Each phase (requirements, design, tasks) requires explicit user approval before moving to the next.
- Spec documents are created and structurally modified via the spec sub-agents (`spec-requirements`, `spec-design`, `spec-tasks`); the main thread only does small edits, renames, and process coordination.
- Mark tasks complete in `tasks.md` as they are implemented; execute one task at a time unless the user requests parallel or automatic execution.
